    "https://careers.dmu.ac.uk/job/People-Operations-Manager/540-en_GB": {
      "title": "People Operations Manager Job Details",
      "description": "People Operations Manager Job Details | demontfort People Operations Manager We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content SEARCH VACANCIES HOW TO APPLY RIGHT TO WORK BENEFITS YOUR DEVELOPMENT VISION EDI LOCATIONS FAQs Search Jobs SEARCH VACANCIES HOW TO APPLY RIGHT TO WORK BENEFITS YOUR DEVELOPMENT VISION EDI LOCATIONS FAQs View profile Job Description Job Alerts Link People Operations Manager Apply now Requisition Id: 540 Job Location: Gateway House Full-time/Part-time: Full-time Employee Weekly Hours: 37.00 Maximum Salary: 56,535.00 GBP Minimum Salary: 44,746.00 GBP Market Supplement: Application Closing Date: 18/10/2026 Job Description: Main duties and responsibilities People Operations Manager (12-month fixed term) De Montfort University is seeking an experienced People Operations Manager to provide leadership and continuity during a 12-month secondment cover period. This is an excellent opportunity for an established HR Operations, Shared Services or People Services leader who enjoys managing teams, delivering operational excellence and improving services in a complex organisation. Leading an experienced team of People Coordinators and an Immigration Adviser, you will be responsible for ensuring the smooth delivery of onboarding, employee lifecycle administration, contractual changes, HR system transactions and immigration operations. You will play a vital role in maintaining service quality, supporting managers and colleagues, and ensuring the University continues to deliver a responsive, customer-focused and compliant people service. What you'll be doing You will: Lead, coach and develop a well-established People Operations team. Create a high-performing culture built on accountability, collaboration and excellent customer service. Oversee operational delivery across onboarding, employee lifecycle processes and HR administration. Ensure work is prioritised effectively and service standards, KPIs and deadlines are consistently achieved. Manage team performance, capacity planning and service resilience. Use operational data and management information to identify trends, risks and opportunities for improvement. Drive continuous improvement of processes, controls and employee experience. Oversee immigration operations and support the University's UKVI sponsor licence responsibilities. Build strong relationships with managers and stakeholders across the University.Support wider People Services priorities and act as deputy to the Head of People Services Operations when required. About you We're looking for a confident and experienced people manager with a strong track record of leading operational HR or People Services teams. You will bring: Significant leadership experience within HR Operations, People Services or Shared Services. Experience managing teams responsible for onboarding, employee lifecycle administration and HR systems. A proven ability to lead, motivate and develop colleagues. Experience managing service delivery, workloads, service standards and operational performance. Strong stakeholder management and relationship-building skills. A continuous improvement mindset and a passion for delivering excellent customer service. Experience working within a large, complex organisation. The confidence to manage competing priorities and resolve operational challenges effectively. Experience of UKVI sponsorship and immigration processes would be advantageous, although candidates with strong HR operations leadership experience are encouraged to apply. To view the job description and person specification, please click here Competencies Team Leadership Resource Allocation Objective Setting Workload Management Employee Development Performance Monitoring Stakeholder Communication Process Improvement Skills Empathy Time Management Conflict Resolution Adaptability Motivation Decision-Making Accountability Honest and Compassionate Innovative and Creative Community Minded Apply now Information at a Glance Share Copy Link Email LinkedIn X Facebook De Montfort University is committed to providing a working and learning environment that enriches lives, supports individuals to reach their full potential, and where everyone is treated with dignity and respect. As an educator and shaper of society, the university aims to role model positive behaviours both within the university and to reflect the diversity of the wider community. As such we welcome applications from all potential candidates. For general enquiries, please contact peopleservices@dmu.ac.uk Accessibility Legal Modern Slavery Act statements Privacy Cookie Consent Manager Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © 2025 De Montfort University × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for