    "https://careers.dmu.ac.uk/job/ProfessorAssociate-Dean-%28Research-And-Innovation%29/681-en_GB": {
      "title": "Professor/Associate Dean (Research And Innovation) Job Details",
      "description": "Professor/Associate Dean (Research And Innovation) Job Details | demontfort We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content SEARCH VACANCIES HOW TO APPLY RIGHT TO WORK BENEFITS YOUR DEVELOPMENT VISION EDI LOCATIONS FAQs Search Jobs SEARCH VACANCIES HOW TO APPLY RIGHT TO WORK BENEFITS YOUR DEVELOPMENT VISION EDI LOCATIONS FAQs View profile Job Description Professor/Associate Dean (Research And Innovation) Apply now Requisition Id: 681 Job Location: Gateway House Full-time/Part-time: Full-time Employee Weekly Hours: 37.00 Maximum Salary: 91,463.00 GBP Minimum Salary: 87,305.00 GBP Market Supplement: Application Closing Date: 02/11/2026 Job Description: Main duties and responsibilities The Role The Associate Dean (Research and Innovation) is a senior leadership role within the Faculty of Technology, Arts and Culture , providing strategic leadership for research, innovation, enterprise and knowledge exchange activities. Reporting to the Dean of Faculty and working closely with the Deputy Vice-Chancellor (Planning, Research and Innovation), the postholder will drive research excellence, innovation and impact across the faculty while fostering a vibrant and sustainable research culture. The Faculty The Faculty of Technology, Arts and Culture is home to a diverse community of academics, researchers, students and external partners committed to delivering impactful research, supporting innovation and enterprise, and contributing to economic, social and cultural development. The Associate Dean will play a pivotal role in advancing the university's strategic ambitions by enhancing research performance, increasing external funding opportunities and strengthening the faculty's reputation nationally and internationally. Key Responsibilities The Associate Dean will lead the development and delivery of the faculty's research and innovation strategy, ensuring alignment with the university's wider objectives. Working closely with colleagues across the institution and external partners, the postholder will support research excellence, increase research income, develop strategic collaborations and create opportunities for innovation, enterprise and knowledge exchange. The role will provide leadership for the faculty's contribution to the Research Excellence Framework (REF), supporting the development of high-quality research outputs, impact and research environment. The successful candidate will encourage interdisciplinary collaboration and help position the faculty to respond effectively to emerging trends and opportunities across the research and innovation landscape. The postholder will also build and strengthen relationships with industry, government, public sector organisations and academic partners, helping to deliver impactful research, commercial activity and knowledge exchange initiatives that enhance the faculty's external profile and contribution to society. As a member of the faculty leadership team, the Associate Dean will provide strategic direction, inspire and support colleagues, and ensure that research and innovation activities are delivered in line with university policies, governance requirements and sector expectations. Why Join Us? This is an exciting opportunity to shape the future of research and innovation within the Faculty of Technology, Arts and Culture and play a leading role in delivering the university's strategic ambitions. Working alongside senior leaders across the institution, you will help drive research excellence, innovation, collaboration and impact for the benefit of our students, staff, partners and wider communities. Interviews will commence on Friday 20th of November. To view the candidate pack please click here Contact For further information regarding the role please contact Shushma Patel - shushma@dmu.ac.uk Apply now Information at a Glance De Montfort University is committed to providing a working and learning environment that enriches lives, supports individuals to reach their full potential, and where everyone is treated with dignity and respect. As an educator and shaper of society, the university aims to role model positive behaviours both within the university and to reflect the diversity of the wider community. As such we welcome applications from all potential candidates. For general enquiries, please contact peopleservices@dmu.ac.uk Accessibility Legal Modern Slavery Act statements Privacy Cookie Consent Manager Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © 2025 De Montfort University × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimising video performance or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these third-parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Functional Cookies Show More Details Functional Cookies Provider Description Enabled YouTube YouTube is a video-sharing service where users can create their own profile, upload videos, watch, like and comment on videos. Opting out of YouTube cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with YouTube videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider YouTube Confirm My Choices Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies"
